lly Wizarding of you know what you  need is a proper one a wand with a core  consisting of hollow-point bullets what  you need sir is a hand cannon the hand  cannon is designed to drop massive  damage in the form of head shots which  fit sportingly with the hit-and-run  style of the Warlock for your special  weapon you should roll with a fusion  rifle that shoots magic or lasers and  quickly annihilates small groups of  low-level enemies or gets rid of one  particularly nasty one think of it as  your best line of defense when  backpedaling from invisible sword  wielding elites or not elites  alternatively if you want to do as much  damage as possible before going in on  your foes and just pack a Pompeii lr3  sniper rifle it fits your Wizarding  lifestyle because it does fire damage  and that is elemental to success haha  finally in the heavy weapons category  you should forego the rocket launchers  and roll with the machine gun remember  the run part of hit-and-run if you find  yourself surrounded by unfriendlies pull  the trigger on this bad boy and don't  stop till it goes click so in conclusion  the warlock class should hang back and  take care of business from cover only  going in to finish bows at the last  possible second with a stiff arm a smart  wizard equip specialty armor to get  their vortex grenade back up and running  as fast as possible make sure also to go  up and frequent our vendors in order to  pick up extra ammo which you'll need if  you plan to take on hard missions also  completing the level 6 strike in the  beta will net you a special wizard  speeder bike which is kind of cool what  are your warlock tips and tricks are you  a hit-and-run type the hang back and  snipe type or something else altogether  let us know your best tactics in the  comments below until then we'll be sure  to work our magic through the power of  interpretive dance in  Maria's places instead  you
 

